1
00:00:00,05 --> 00:00:02,02
- [Instructor] We have seen with multiple examples

2
00:00:02,02 --> 00:00:03,04
how to manage the states

3
00:00:03,04 --> 00:00:06,08
with the React API with useState, with useReducer

4
00:00:06,08 --> 00:00:08,05
and also useContext.

5
00:00:08,05 --> 00:00:10,07
With useState, you can create local state variables

6
00:00:10,07 --> 00:00:13,04
that remain attached to one component only.

7
00:00:13,04 --> 00:00:16,03
And with useReducer, you can manage complex logic separate

8
00:00:16,03 --> 00:00:17,06
from one component.

9
00:00:17,06 --> 00:00:20,05
And useContext allows to create and share global state

10
00:00:20,05 --> 00:00:22,06
without having to pass data down manually

11
00:00:22,06 --> 00:00:25,07
from top to bottom with one single source of truth.

12
00:00:25,07 --> 00:00:28,01
So every hook has its own benefits.

13
00:00:28,01 --> 00:00:30,04
The React API has certain limitations though.

14
00:00:30,04 --> 00:00:32,07
For example, component state can only be shared

15
00:00:32,07 --> 00:00:35,04
by pushing it up to the common ancestor.

16
00:00:35,04 --> 00:00:38,01
And that is the same challenge as with props really,

17
00:00:38,01 --> 00:00:39,05
meaning that the state is kept

18
00:00:39,05 --> 00:00:43,00
in one location to pass data down from top to bottom,

19
00:00:43,00 --> 00:00:45,06
which is not very flexible.

20
00:00:45,06 --> 00:00:48,06
And with context, you can only store one single value.

21
00:00:48,06 --> 00:00:50,09
These limitations make it difficult to split the code

22
00:00:50,09 --> 00:00:52,09
from the tree where the state leaves

23
00:00:52,09 --> 00:00:54,06
from the leaves of the tree.

24
00:00:54,06 --> 00:00:56,02
By leaves, I mean the components

25
00:00:56,02 --> 00:00:58,06
where the state is consumed.

26
00:00:58,06 --> 00:01:01,01
To go beyond the limitations of the React API,

27
00:01:01,01 --> 00:01:04,02
new solutions like Recoil comes in very handy.

28
00:01:04,02 --> 00:01:05,06
Recoil acts like React

29
00:01:05,06 --> 00:01:08,04
with a seamless syntax, semantic and behavior

30
00:01:08,04 --> 00:01:12,00
but with more capabilities and Recoil has the same simple

31
00:01:12,00 --> 00:01:15,03
and minimal interface as with React with the get and sets.

32
00:01:15,03 --> 00:01:19,08
So let me explain to you how it works.

33
00:01:19,08 --> 00:01:22,01
Recoil is using atomic approach,

34
00:01:22,01 --> 00:01:24,02
meaning that developers can define atoms

35
00:01:24,02 --> 00:01:26,07
that represents pieces of data.

36
00:01:26,07 --> 00:01:27,06
And so the atoms

37
00:01:27,06 --> 00:01:30,07
are like independent objects containing the data.

38
00:01:30,07 --> 00:01:33,05
Then the data is shared down into React components

39
00:01:33,05 --> 00:01:37,04
through selectors, which are pure functions.

40
00:01:37,04 --> 00:01:39,02
The library also provide with hooks

41
00:01:39,02 --> 00:01:40,07
that makes it easy to access

42
00:01:40,07 --> 00:01:43,06
and update the state from within React components.

43
00:01:43,06 --> 00:01:45,05
So let's begin with a new example.

44
00:01:45,05 --> 00:01:48,05
In the next example, we are building a to-do list.

45
00:01:48,05 --> 00:01:49,08
The features are very simple.

46
00:01:49,08 --> 00:01:51,05
We're going to have a list of items

47
00:01:51,05 --> 00:01:55,00
and we have also the options to add new items

48
00:01:55,00 --> 00:01:57,01
with options also to filter the list.

49
00:01:57,01 --> 00:02:00,07
So we also enable the feature to cross items off the list

50
00:02:00,07 --> 00:02:03,02
so to indicate that this is completed.

51
00:02:03,02 --> 00:02:06,02
Then you can also delete the items that are completed

52
00:02:06,02 --> 00:02:08,02
and decide to only filter

53
00:02:08,02 --> 00:02:11,04
and display the items that are completed.

54
00:02:11,04 --> 00:02:15,01
So this is a very basic example built with the React API.

55
00:02:15,01 --> 00:02:16,06
Here the challenge is the same.

56
00:02:16,06 --> 00:02:19,04
If you ever need to scale the app, you need an efficient way

57
00:02:19,04 --> 00:02:22,06
to share data between components without making components

58
00:02:22,06 --> 00:02:24,02
depending on each other.

59
00:02:24,02 --> 00:02:26,07
So the first step is to make the application aware

60
00:02:26,07 --> 00:02:28,06
of the state with RecoilRoot.

61
00:02:28,06 --> 00:02:30,03
RecoilRoot is an important component

62
00:02:30,03 --> 00:02:31,08
of the Recoil library.

63
00:02:31,08 --> 00:02:33,09
It is a component that provides the context

64
00:02:33,09 --> 00:02:37,01
in which atoms have values, and it must be apparent

65
00:02:37,01 --> 00:02:40,01
of any component that uses any Recoil hook.

66
00:02:40,01 --> 00:02:41,05
I will show you how.

67
00:02:41,05 --> 00:02:45,08
First we want to make sure that we install the Recoil library.

68
00:02:45,08 --> 00:02:50,07
Then we go into our projects.

69
00:02:50,07 --> 00:02:52,01
Right here.

70
00:02:52,01 --> 00:02:57,01
We're going to make sure that first we install Recoil.

71
00:02:57,01 --> 00:03:00,05
So it looks like this is not possible to actually paste.

72
00:03:00,05 --> 00:03:05,04
So I'm going to do npm i and recoil.

73
00:03:05,04 --> 00:03:09,01
And next, while this is being installed,

74
00:03:09,01 --> 00:03:13,00
I'm just going to grab, so let's go back to RecoilRoot.

75
00:03:13,00 --> 00:03:15,03
And the way it should be is that you're going to add

76
00:03:15,03 --> 00:03:19,08
to the scope of your entry point in your React project

77
00:03:19,08 --> 00:03:22,07
and make sure that you wrap the app components.

78
00:03:22,07 --> 00:03:25,08
So the root component with the RecoilRoot component.

79
00:03:25,08 --> 00:03:26,08
Okay, so this is done.

80
00:03:26,08 --> 00:03:32,09
So let's go find the index.js,

81
00:03:32,09 --> 00:03:35,02
add this to the scope like this

82
00:03:35,02 --> 00:03:38,03
and we're going to wrap the root component with RecoilRoot.

83
00:03:38,03 --> 00:03:39,07
That's going to be the first step

84
00:03:39,07 --> 00:03:43,07
in order to make any descending component aware

85
00:03:43,07 --> 00:03:45,02
of the context.

86
00:03:45,02 --> 00:03:47,05
And so any descending component can access

87
00:03:47,05 --> 00:03:49,03
and update the state

88
00:03:49,03 --> 00:03:52,01
by accessing the state through the RecoilRoot.

89
00:03:52,01 --> 00:03:53,01
So in a nutshell,

90
00:03:53,01 --> 00:03:55,08
Recoil is a tool that helps developers manage the state

91
00:03:55,08 --> 00:03:58,08
in their React applications, making it easier

92
00:03:58,08 --> 00:04:01,09
to build complex and robust user interfaces.

93
00:04:01,09 --> 00:04:03,01
Coming next, we're going to see

94
00:04:03,01 --> 00:04:05,09
how to divide the state management by using atoms.

95
00:04:05,09 --> 00:04:08,01
So we're going to see how to create atoms

96
00:04:08,01 --> 00:04:11,07
that are independent objects containing the state

97
00:04:11,07 --> 00:04:13,00
of your app.

